abstract: >-
  Newman's conjecture that the de Bruijn-Newman constant is non-negative, proved by Rodgers and Tao in 2018,
  is formalized in Lean 4 along Dobner's 2020 proof: for every t < 0 the heat-flowed Riemann xi function H_t
  has a non-real zero. The proof term depends only on propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound; it was read
  back independently, granted through the Arda registry gate, and replayed by two kernels (Lean, nanoda) via
  Comparator against a challenge whose type is the registered statement. New kernel-checked infrastructure:
  complex Stirling with explicit remainder, the digamma asymptotic, Bohr almost periodicity for everywhere
  convergent Dirichlet series, the Gaussian-convolution representation of H_t, and a saddle-point analysis.
  Together with the registry's Lambda <= 9/32 the kernel-checked range is 0 <= Lambda <= 9/32; Lambda = 0 is
  the Riemann Hypothesis and is not proved.
